      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need help writing a rejection email for a candidate. they made it to the final round for a senior dev role here in austin but we decided to go with someone else. they were actually really good and had great technical skills, so i want the email to be professional and kind but still clear that we aren't moving forward. can u help me draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you draft a rejection email that's both professional and kind. Here's a sample:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were impressed by your exceptional technical skills and the time you took to showcase your expertise during the final round of interviews. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience align more closely with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were truly impressed by your qualifications and passion for software development. Your contributions to the final round of interviews were invaluable, and we appreciate the time and effort you invested in our process.\n\nWe appreciate your interest in joining our team and wish you the best of luck in your ongoing job search. We have no doubt that your skills and experience will serve you well in your future endeavors.\n\nThank you again for your interest in [Company Name], and we wish you continued success.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\"\n\nI hope this sample helps you draft a rejection email that's both professional and kind. You can always adjust it to fit your company's tone and style.",
